   "text": "Write a resume for a junior hardware engineer. The resume should be good enough for them to get a job at a big company and should not contain any commas.\n\n---\n\n**Name:** [Insert Name]  \n**Contact Information:** [Insert Email] | [Insert Phone Number] | [Insert LinkedIn Profile] | [Insert GitHub Profile]  \n**Location:** [Insert City, State, Country]  \n**Date of Birth:** [Insert Date of Birth]  \n**Gender:** [Insert Gender]  \n**Education:** [Insert Degree, University, Graduation Date]  \n**Certifications:** [Insert Certifications, if any]  \n\n---\n\n*Highlighted Section: Professional Experience*  \n**Junior Hardware Engineer**  \n[Company Name], [City, State] | [Start Date – End Date]  \n- Designed and implemented hardware solutions for [specific project or product]  \n- Conducted circuit design and testing using [specific tools or software]  \n- Collaborated with software teams to integrate hardware components  \n- Documented and maintained hardware specifications and schematics  \n- Troubleshooted and resolved hardware issues in production environments  \n- Participated in hardware development lifecycle from concept to deployment  \n\n---\n\n*Highlighted Section: Projects*  \n- [Project Name 1] | [Duration]  \n  - Described the project and responsibilities  \n- [Project Name 2] | [Duration]  \n  - Described the project and responsibilities  \n\n---\n\n*Highlighted Section: Skills*  \n- Hardware Design  \n- Circuit Layout  \n- PCB Design  \n- Schematic Capture  \n- Embedded Systems  \n- Troubleshooting  \n- CAD Software (e.g. Altium, EAGLE)  \n- Programming (e.g. C, C++, Python)  \n- Communication  \n- Teamwork  \n- Problem Solving  \n\n---\n\n*Highlighted Section: Languages*  \n- English (Fluent)  \n- [Other Language, if applicable]  \n\n---\n\n*Highlighted Section: Additional Information*  \n- [Insert any relevant projects, internships, or certifications]  \n- [Insert any relevant volunteer work or extracurricular activities]  \n\n--- \n\nLet me know if you'd like this resume formatted in a specific way or with more details.",
